# Copy to torrent/transmission.env (gitignored) and fill in, then:
#   chmod 600 torrent/transmission.env
#
#   cp torrent/transmission.env.example torrent/transmission.env
#
# THIS FILE IS A CONTRACT, NOT A DOC — these key names are what the
# linuxserver/transmission image reads to configure RPC auth.
#
# Set these via env, NEVER by hand-editing /config/settings.json: the image's own
# documentation warns that credentials written directly into settings.json stop
# transmission from being shut down cleanly by the s6 supervisor.
#
# The tailnet is already an authentication boundary, so this password is defence
# in depth, not the only lock — but set a real one anyway. Anything on the tailnet
# (a phone, a laptop, a guest device you added once) can reach the UI.

# Web UI / RPC username.
USER=

# Web UI / RPC password. Generate one rather than choosing one, e.g.:
#   openssl rand -base64 24
PASS=
